.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-CREATE-QUEUE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-create-queue \- create a new queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs create-queue
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
[\fB\-\-visibility\fR|\fB\-v\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR|\fB\-m\fR \fICOUNT\fR]
[\fB\-\-max\-length\fR|\fB\-l\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
[\fB\-\-dlq\-name\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-delay\fR|\fB\-e\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new queue with the given name, max retries, max message
length, dead letter queue name, and visibility timeout. The dead letter
queue name is optional.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the queue to create. Required.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-visibility " " \fISECONDS\fR
Visibility timeout applied to received messages, in seconds. Defaults
to \fI30\fR.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-retries " " \fICOUNT\fR
Maximum number of times a message may be received before it is moved
to the dead letter queue (if any). Defaults to \fI3\fR.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-max\-length " " \fIBYTES\fR
Maximum message body length, in bytes. Defaults to \fI1048576\fR (1 MiB).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dlq\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name of an existing queue to use as the dead letter queue. Optional; if
omitted, messages that exceed \fB\-\-max\-retries\fR are dropped.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-delay " " \fISECONDS\fR
Delay before newly sent messages become visible to receivers. Defaults
to \fI0\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The queue was created; its ERN and other metadata are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or the
server rejected the request (e.g. a queue with that name already
exists, or \fB\-\-dlq\-name\fR does not refer to an existing queue).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs create-queue \e
    --name orders --visibility 30 --max-retries 3 --max-length 65536

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs create-queue \e
    --name orders --dlq-name orders-dlq --delay 5
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
